releases.notes:
With the improvements around MixinSquared all now used, I Can't Believe It's Not 1.21.5 is in fit shape for use both in production and development. Capable of loading popular 1.21.5 mods such as [REI](https://modrinth.com/mod/rei) and [Tech Reborn](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/techreborn) on 25w14craftmine with only minor manual [`fabric_mod_dependencies.json`](https://fabricmc.net/wiki/tutorial:dependency_overrides) additions to override Minecraft version dependency checks in mods which explicitly restrict their support to 1.21.5 only.

![2025-04-09_01 24 15](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/edbb6b6d-c3fb-4124-ad7d-8a31ad317772)

For creative mode fans, creating a new world in creative has been made possible again with the re-addition of creative in the game mode selector button.

The player unlocks button has also been added to the creative inventory screen - there is even provision for REI to draw around (rather than over) it:

![2025-04-11_18 56 13](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1480310c-d8ef-4ff2-95de-00b6ff9db0da)

---

As an example for using I Can't Believe It's Not 1.21.5, in this case with REI and Tech Reborn, the following needs to be put in a file named `fabric_loader_dependencies.json` in the `config` folder:
```json
{
	"version": 1,
	"overrides": {
		"techreborn": {
			"-depends": {
				"minecraft": "Converted"
			}
		},
		"reborncore": {
			"-depends": {
				"minecraft": "Converted"
			}
		}
	}
}
```
You'll notice that there is nothing for REI, which is because it works right out of the box.

Other than this it's as simple as adding the 1.21.5 mods to the mods folder, you Won't Believe It's Not 1.21.5
